WEBVTT

00:10.636 --> 00:12.638
[wind howling]

00:23.357 --> 00:25.359
[groaning]

00:32.698 --> 00:34.701
[grunting]

00:45.754 --> 00:46.880
[laughs]

00:59.059 --> 01:00.936
[phone ringing]

01:08.735 --> 01:09.736
[Tom] Issue this.

01:11.738 --> 01:13.323
But what about the fireworks?

01:15.117 --> 01:16.159
Do it.

01:24.251 --> 01:25.878
Hey, Ruth. Um…

01:27.379 --> 01:29.423
I'm gonna need you here today.

01:30.340 --> 01:32.843
Absolutely. I just need to leave at 3:00.

01:32.926 --> 01:36.763
Ah, no. [stutters]
That is exactly what I mean. Okay.

01:39.725 --> 01:42.019
This is insane,
you can't just lock me in here.

01:42.769 --> 01:44.479
I don't have time to relitigate this.

01:44.563 --> 01:47.816
I'm gonna be gone for 30 minutes.
You need a snack, ask Ruth.

01:50.777 --> 01:53.488
I can see you calculating how much
you think you can get away with

01:53.572 --> 01:56.366
in 30 minutes. So how about this,
I'm gonna call every ten.

01:57.951 --> 02:00.037
What do I do? Do I just, um… [sighs]

02:00.120 --> 02:03.749
I press a button and then, like…

02:03.832 --> 02:05.959
How… What… How do I… What's the system?

02:06.585 --> 02:08.586
The system is you pick up
the goddamn phone.

02:08.669 --> 02:10.672
I didn't know we were swearing now.

02:11.673 --> 02:14.343
Hey, is it true that Reverend Bryce
hung himself?

02:17.054 --> 02:18.180
Wasn't he your friend?

02:24.770 --> 02:26.605
We'll talk about it when I get back.

02:37.199 --> 02:39.201
[organ music playing]

02:47.209 --> 02:51.296
[townsperson] I don't get it. I saw him
at The Rye just a few weeks ago.

02:52.005 --> 02:53.674
He was getting a coffee.

02:54.925 --> 02:56.009
I think.

02:56.760 --> 02:58.804
Maybe not. We didn't talk.

02:59.555 --> 03:01.598
I didn't really know him anyway.

03:03.475 --> 03:05.477
[microphone rustling]

03:07.354 --> 03:08.647
[officiant] Thank you, Paul.

03:09.439 --> 03:13.861
Once again, I'd like to remind everyone
that it is not mandatory that you speak.

03:31.086 --> 03:32.629
[Wyck hums]

03:32.713 --> 03:33.714
[grunts]

03:38.051 --> 03:39.970
[Patricia sighs] There's nothing.

03:41.305 --> 03:43.140
[Wyck] Ah, there's always something.

03:44.558 --> 03:46.310
[Patricia] What the hell happened here?

03:46.393 --> 03:48.145
And why would he burn everything?

03:48.228 --> 03:50.606
[Wyck] Just save every scrap you can.

03:53.901 --> 03:55.194
Hmm. All right.

03:55.777 --> 03:58.989
Need to tell people what's going on
or they're gonna start getting killed.

04:01.658 --> 04:03.911
- I'm trying to get things under control.
- Yep.

04:03.994 --> 04:08.081
Your little curfew isn't gonna do it.
You can't even control your own son.

04:08.165 --> 04:10.334
[Patricia] Okay. Okay. Okay.

04:11.126 --> 04:12.127
[sighs]

04:14.922 --> 04:15.923
[softly] All right.

04:32.147 --> 04:33.482
What's wrong?

04:34.691 --> 04:36.068
[Tom sighs]

04:36.985 --> 04:37.986
He…

04:38.070 --> 04:39.571
He tried to call me.

04:42.658 --> 04:44.117
[keypad beeping]

04:44.201 --> 04:45.494
And another number.

04:47.788 --> 04:48.789
A lot.

04:48.872 --> 04:49.873
[Wyck] Dial it.

04:51.208 --> 04:52.960
[keypad beeping]

04:56.588 --> 04:58.882
[dial tone]

04:58.966 --> 05:01.677
[line beeping, rings]

05:01.760 --> 05:02.886
[person] Hello?

05:04.429 --> 05:06.348
[stammers] Hi. Yes, um…

05:08.100 --> 05:09.434
Who-Who is this?

05:09.518 --> 05:10.686
[person] Who is this?

05:10.769 --> 05:12.855
[Tom] Uh, sorry. I just, I just…

05:13.355 --> 05:16.066
I found your number in my phone, and I--

05:16.149 --> 05:17.484
- [line disconnects]
- Fuck.

05:17.568 --> 05:18.569
[sighs]

05:20.195 --> 05:21.405
You try.

05:21.905 --> 05:23.532
- [Tom] Yes!
- He won't pick up.

05:23.615 --> 05:25.158
The call's coming from the same number.

05:25.242 --> 05:27.202
[line beeping, rings]

05:27.286 --> 05:28.495
[person] Hello?

05:28.579 --> 05:29.705
Hi. How are you?

05:30.873 --> 05:32.040
Good.

05:35.711 --> 05:37.379
Reverend Bryce gave me your number.

05:38.046 --> 05:39.673
Would you like an appointment?

05:40.632 --> 05:42.551
- [mouthing] Yes.
- [smacks lips] Yes I would.

05:43.051 --> 05:45.345
- Give me fifteen minutes.
- [Patricia] Oh. Uh… Uh…

05:45.429 --> 05:46.847
That's… Okay. Where are you?

05:51.268 --> 05:52.269
12 Birch Street.

05:52.352 --> 05:54.354
[mysterious music playing]

06:05.866 --> 06:06.867
[knocks on door]

06:07.367 --> 06:08.368
[person] Come in!

06:15.792 --> 06:17.503
[music fades]

06:18.795 --> 06:19.796
[sniffs]

06:21.089 --> 06:22.090
[Patricia whispers] Hey.

06:29.723 --> 06:30.724
Thank you.

06:36.897 --> 06:37.898
This feels good.

06:42.319 --> 06:43.320
Okay.

06:51.286 --> 06:52.287
What's it gonna be?

07:02.297 --> 07:03.298
Hmm.

07:05.509 --> 07:07.094
[clicks tongue] Who we got here?

07:10.681 --> 07:12.683
[exhaling deeply]

07:13.809 --> 07:15.102
Hello again.

07:16.436 --> 07:18.355
That is a brutal fucking ride.

07:18.438 --> 07:19.606
Damn, Papa.

07:21.149 --> 07:23.193
[chuckles]

07:23.277 --> 07:24.278
Todd O'Connor?

07:25.320 --> 07:26.738
Hey, Patty. How you doin'?

07:26.822 --> 07:27.990
Yeah. Good thanks.

07:28.532 --> 07:31.243
- Oh, my God. You're a drug dealer.
- No, no. No, please.

07:31.326 --> 07:32.327
I'm a shaman.

07:32.828 --> 07:34.037
[Patricia] Is that cocaine?

07:34.121 --> 07:35.122
Yes.

07:36.331 --> 07:38.417
Todd and I went to school together.
We were like--

07:38.500 --> 07:40.002
What are… What are these?

07:40.085 --> 07:44.923
That, my friend, is the one fucking
mushroom I'm not going near.

07:45.007 --> 07:48.135
Dude, that shit is gonna take you
where you gotta go,

07:48.218 --> 07:50.804
regardless of if you wanna go there.

07:50.888 --> 07:52.806
Old timers call that thing Truesight.

07:53.473 --> 07:55.225
Only grows here local on the island.

07:55.309 --> 07:57.227
Imagine getting LASIK for your third eye.

07:57.311 --> 07:58.896
Blasts that thing open.

07:58.979 --> 07:59.980
Pow!

08:01.940 --> 08:06.862
I'm sorry, I'm-I'm trying to figure out
why Reverend Bryce would take it?

08:06.945 --> 08:08.363
Well, he was looking for answers.

08:08.447 --> 08:09.531
He hung himself.

08:11.241 --> 08:12.242
[sighs]

08:12.326 --> 08:13.327
Shit.

08:18.290 --> 08:20.292
Uh, I guess he didn't like the answers.

08:21.293 --> 08:22.294
Damn.

08:22.794 --> 08:24.922
You know, I-I have a buddy who took it.

08:25.005 --> 08:26.298
You remember Brian Morrison?

08:26.381 --> 08:28.091
"Bri Guy"?
Stole his mom's car in eighth grade?

08:28.175 --> 08:30.511
- Mm-hmm.
- Flipped it in the woods? Maniac.

08:30.594 --> 08:34.306
Anyway, Brian saw something on his trip
that changed him completely.

08:34.890 --> 08:37.392
He encountered something
he wouldn't talk about.

08:37.476 --> 08:40.187
But he chilled out majorly afterwards.

08:40.270 --> 08:43.232
Stopped getting into fights,
stopped yelling at his girl.

08:44.149 --> 08:45.526
She had to feed him though.

08:45.609 --> 08:47.611
He lost some pretty major motor skills.

08:48.612 --> 08:50.280
Happy guy though. [sighs]

08:50.781 --> 08:52.908
Just hard for her
to get him down at night.

08:52.991 --> 08:59.331
Anyway, he drew the same thing
over, and over, and over again.

08:59.414 --> 09:02.835
I think he saw it on his trip.
I have one of them, lying around here.

09:04.419 --> 09:06.797
It's kinda ancient…

09:07.965 --> 09:10.676
vaguely religious iconography.

09:10.759 --> 09:14.096
It's the kind of sacred geometry
you don't just riff.

09:19.101 --> 09:20.102
Yeah, man.

09:20.811 --> 09:23.522
Yeah, take that in. [exhales deeply]

09:24.147 --> 09:26.275
- Some doors are meant to stay shut.
- Oh, yeah.

09:26.358 --> 09:27.609
Am I right, folks?

09:28.360 --> 09:29.444
How do you take it?

09:31.071 --> 09:34.533
Well, I can make you a tincture
for 35 bucks, if that's amenable?

09:34.616 --> 09:36.702
- No, thanks.
- You and your companions can hang out

09:36.785 --> 09:38.453
in the Peace Center
at no extra cost to you.

09:38.537 --> 09:39.538
Do it.

09:41.957 --> 09:43.125
Okay.

09:43.834 --> 09:45.335
Would you excuse us for a minute?

09:45.419 --> 09:48.380
[Todd] Yeah, yeah. There's no rush
to the augmentation of the soul, folks.

09:48.922 --> 09:51.175
This fungus doesn't hold the secrets
of the island.

09:51.258 --> 09:52.885
It's gonna leave you muttering
in a corner.

09:52.968 --> 09:55.304
Look, if you don't want to take
the scary mushroom,

09:55.387 --> 09:57.723
after bringing all these tourists here
to the island,

09:57.806 --> 09:59.850
that's for you to live with.

10:14.156 --> 10:15.240
Wyck will take it.

10:16.325 --> 10:17.326
[Todd] Very cool.

10:18.035 --> 10:19.786
No. Of course there's not gonna be
fireworks.

10:19.870 --> 10:21.788
Which part of "curfew"
do they not understand?

10:21.872 --> 10:25.042
[Dale] Listen, I think you should know
that people are angry.

10:25.125 --> 10:29.296
Apparently Kurt is gathering a meeting.
Trying to overturn your curfew.

10:29.379 --> 10:32.633
- [whimsical music playing on radio]
- I'll be back in 15 minutes.

10:33.258 --> 10:34.551
Damn it.

10:36.887 --> 10:38.305
- I've gotta get back.
- Uh-huh.

10:38.388 --> 10:39.640
I'll stay with him.

10:39.723 --> 10:42.643
- You sure you wanna do this?
- The only way out is through.

10:42.726 --> 10:44.728
[Tom] I-I know, but it's jus…
I don't know.

10:44.811 --> 10:47.898
[groans] Oh, God.
It… it even looks hideous.

10:48.690 --> 10:50.275
But you can't taste it, right?

10:50.359 --> 10:51.360
What?

10:51.443 --> 10:52.653
[grunts]

10:56.156 --> 10:57.157
[Tom gulps]

10:58.742 --> 11:01.620
It… it's in here?

11:02.412 --> 11:03.580
Mm-hmm.

11:07.292 --> 11:10.921
We-We-We s… We said Wyck
was-was gonna take it.

11:11.004 --> 11:12.256
Yeah. You're Wyck.

11:13.882 --> 11:17.469
- Oh, my God. Oh-Oh-Oh, my God!
- [Todd] It's okay, it's okay.

11:17.553 --> 11:20.472
- Just-Just sip it slowly.
- What? I finished it!

11:20.556 --> 11:22.015
- Ah.
- [Tom] I ca… I can't be on this!

11:22.099 --> 11:23.183
I-I can't be on this!

11:23.267 --> 11:24.726
Not now! Now today!

11:24.810 --> 11:26.061
Make yourself throw up.

11:26.144 --> 11:27.187
- I can't!
- [Todd] Stay calm.

11:27.271 --> 11:30.357
- It's only a 12 hour experience.
- Oh, my God!

11:30.440 --> 11:31.567
- Oh, my God!
- [Patricia] Tom…

11:31.650 --> 11:33.777
Oh, my God. Oh, my… Oh, my God.

11:33.861 --> 11:35.487
[Todd] It really is best to purge!

11:37.823 --> 11:39.741
[gags] I can't throw up.
I've never been able to.

11:39.825 --> 11:42.077
- [Patricia] Here.
- [gagging] Stop, stop!

11:42.160 --> 11:43.871
- Oh, come on, Tom. Shush!
- [gags, whimpers]

11:43.954 --> 11:45.372
Stop, stop, stop, stop!

11:46.290 --> 11:47.749
Oh, my God. Evan.

11:48.625 --> 11:50.002
What am I gonna do about Evan?

11:50.586 --> 11:52.171
Don't worry. I'm on it.

11:53.088 --> 11:54.590
What? What are you gonna do?

11:55.090 --> 11:57.092
[whimsical music continues]

11:59.261 --> 12:00.971
- [music stops]
- [Todd] Careful here. Okay.

12:01.054 --> 12:03.515
And we're just gonna wind down here
in the Peace Center.

12:05.100 --> 12:06.310
That's good.

12:06.393 --> 12:09.438
Let's have a seat. On the mindfulness bed.

12:09.521 --> 12:11.190
Per… yeah. That's it. Yep.

12:11.273 --> 12:13.567
And let's get fully supine. Yep.

12:13.650 --> 12:16.278
[whispering] And here we go.

12:17.821 --> 12:20.532
Oh. I'm so sorry.
I didn't realize she'd gotten out.

12:20.616 --> 12:21.992
Come here, Bridget.

12:22.075 --> 12:25.120
She's turning 50 soon,
so she's got wanderlust.

12:25.704 --> 12:28.498
Tom. Tom! Listen to me.

12:28.582 --> 12:30.125
Listen to me. Sit. Sit.

12:30.751 --> 12:33.921
Now, don't squander this.

12:34.505 --> 12:36.590
You find those answers, now.

12:36.673 --> 12:37.674
- What?
- Yeah.

12:38.342 --> 12:40.219
Good news. Um…

12:40.302 --> 12:43.096
Evan is fine, and he's gonna stay
at Ruth's.

12:43.180 --> 12:44.932
Oh, thank God. Who'd you talk to?

12:45.015 --> 12:46.558
- Evan.
- Oh, my God.

12:46.642 --> 12:48.018
- I have to get back.
- [Wyck] Tom.

12:48.101 --> 12:51.104
I think we just ride it out here.
He seems to know what he's doing.

12:51.188 --> 12:53.440
- Yeah.
- Don't you think it's best to stay here?

12:53.524 --> 12:56.276
Absolutely. I do personally have to go.

12:56.360 --> 12:58.028
As my girlfriend's cat has absconded.

12:58.111 --> 13:00.030
But in the meantime
you can totally guide him.

13:00.113 --> 13:01.740
- What?
- [Todd] Just stay calm.

13:01.823 --> 13:05.661
And whatever you do, do not look
at any mirrors.

13:05.744 --> 13:07.079
You got this, Wyck.

13:09.373 --> 13:12.084
What do I do if you freak-out?
What do I do if you freak-out?

13:12.167 --> 13:13.710
Take me back to the office right now.

13:13.794 --> 13:17.256
- [Wyck] Have you seen anything?
- Take me back to the office. Now.

13:19.925 --> 13:20.926
[gasps]

13:21.009 --> 13:22.636
Just stop yelling at me.

13:24.179 --> 13:25.305
How did we get here?

13:25.389 --> 13:26.515
Where's Wyck?

13:27.349 --> 13:28.809
You told him he could go.

13:29.393 --> 13:31.270
He said he was gonna find the answers
you won't.

13:31.353 --> 13:33.814
[echoing] I-I don't know what
that means but…

13:34.314 --> 13:35.315
Do you hear that?

13:38.235 --> 13:40.153
[Tom yells, inhales sharply]

13:42.531 --> 13:44.157
[Patricia] Just give me a name, Tom.

13:44.783 --> 13:47.369
Where's Evan? W-W-Where is my son?

13:47.452 --> 13:49.705
[sighs] For the third time.

13:50.205 --> 13:51.206
[sighs]

13:51.957 --> 13:53.000
Evan is not here.

13:54.376 --> 13:56.336
But we're gonna find him.

13:57.087 --> 13:58.547
Who's that kid he runs with?

13:59.631 --> 14:00.632
PJ Glanville?

14:00.716 --> 14:02.843
PJ Glanville is an awful, awful…

14:02.926 --> 14:04.386
[Patricia sighs]

14:04.469 --> 14:05.470
…boy.

14:05.554 --> 14:07.556
[liquid gurgling, echoing]

14:08.932 --> 14:10.100
Do you hear that sound?

14:10.184 --> 14:13.854
[sighs] No, Tom. I don't hear the sound.

14:14.354 --> 14:16.732
Just take a deep breath.

14:18.984 --> 14:20.194
[breathes sharply]

14:20.277 --> 14:22.654
- What's wrong with him?
- [exhales deeply]

14:22.738 --> 14:25.073
Oh, nothing. He's, um… uh, just…

14:25.616 --> 14:27.534
Here. Hold your organizer.

14:27.618 --> 14:29.995
He-He doesn't know how dangerous
it is out there.

14:31.371 --> 14:33.498
P-Patricia, he does… Can you hear me?

14:33.582 --> 14:35.417
He doesn't know how dangerous
it is out there!

14:36.835 --> 14:37.920
- Hi, there.
- [Tom screams]

14:38.003 --> 14:39.254
Oh, God!

14:40.255 --> 14:42.424
[rap music playing on radio]

14:42.508 --> 14:44.468
[PJ] You girls gotta be careful
around here.

14:44.551 --> 14:45.802
- [teen 1] Why?
- [teen 2] Why?

14:47.471 --> 14:49.681
The house there. The…

14:49.765 --> 14:52.392
Back in the day these girls
used to get these hang up calls.

14:53.143 --> 14:54.937
- [coughs]
- Um…

14:55.020 --> 14:57.606
And turns out it was coming from the guy
who lived here.

14:57.689 --> 15:01.360
He, like, lost his mind,

15:01.443 --> 15:05.280
and one night just went out
and stabbed a bunch of bitches.

15:05.364 --> 15:07.241
Bitches? Really?

15:07.324 --> 15:09.576
Sorry, your majesty,
he stabbed a bunch of young women.

15:09.660 --> 15:10.744
[teen 2] Hmm. Thank you.

15:10.827 --> 15:12.162
[PJ] Um, I'm serious. They…

15:12.246 --> 15:16.375
My uncle told me they tried to kill him.
I guess they called him the-the Boogeyman.

15:16.458 --> 15:19.127
And they shot him and he wouldn't die.

15:19.211 --> 15:20.587
And so they, um…

15:21.755 --> 15:23.715
they, like, buried him in the basement

15:23.799 --> 15:25.968
and they sealed the whole thing
in concrete.

15:26.051 --> 15:27.344
- Is he being serious?
- Yeah.

15:27.427 --> 15:29.763
You gotta be quiet around here,
you don't know…

15:31.431 --> 15:32.975
you don't know what's gonna happen.

15:33.058 --> 15:35.352
[ominous music playing]

15:38.397 --> 15:39.857
- [horn blares]
- [exclaiming]

15:39.940 --> 15:41.567
- Jesus Christ, dude!
- [laughing]

15:41.650 --> 15:42.693
- Jesus Christ!
- [teen 2] God!

15:42.776 --> 15:43.902
- Sorry.
- What's wrong with you?

15:43.986 --> 15:45.737
- Oh, my God.
- [PJ] Okay, guys, we can be friends,

15:45.821 --> 15:48.031
and we can smoke pot, and we can make
each other laugh, you know?

15:48.115 --> 15:51.243
[Patricia chuckles] Okay.
Well, just let me know if he turns up.

15:51.326 --> 15:52.411
Thank you so much.

15:53.912 --> 15:55.205
Aw, she was nice.

15:57.207 --> 15:58.500
Oh, God.

15:59.459 --> 16:00.586
[door closes]

16:00.669 --> 16:03.505
Uh… [clears throat]
…were you gonna tell me?

16:05.841 --> 16:06.925
The curfew?

16:07.426 --> 16:10.262
See, I've got a cell that holds six,

16:10.345 --> 16:14.057
so when I go out tonight and see literally
everyone walking around…

16:14.141 --> 16:17.519
[distorted] …which I will,
because there are fireworks tonight,

16:17.603 --> 16:19.730
which six people do you
want me to pick up?

16:20.689 --> 16:22.524
[normal] Huh? Huh, talk me through that.

16:22.608 --> 16:24.109
Tell me how you see that happening.

16:27.029 --> 16:29.615
Okay, so I can see you've given this
a lot of thought. Okay, good.

16:29.698 --> 16:31.033
- Uh, Patricia, come on.
- Huh?

16:31.116 --> 16:32.701
Uh, we're going down to the station.

16:32.784 --> 16:34.578
Me? Why?

16:34.661 --> 16:36.622
Well, I gotta take down your statement.

16:38.415 --> 16:40.334
- Can it wait?
- No, it cannot,

16:40.417 --> 16:44.296
because some people who woke up
in the sea last night wanna press charges.

16:44.379 --> 16:45.380
[sighs, stammers]

16:45.464 --> 16:47.174
Okay, okay. [huffs]

16:47.799 --> 16:51.178
I guess I'll be right back,
so, uh, you just sit here.

16:52.012 --> 16:53.013
Right?

16:54.056 --> 16:55.057
[grunts]

16:56.058 --> 16:57.100
Don't open the door.

17:10.113 --> 17:13.909
[people chattering]

17:18.204 --> 17:20.290
- [phone ringing]
- [chattering continues]

17:20.874 --> 17:22.876
[gentle music playing]

17:23.377 --> 17:24.377
Ger.

17:25.295 --> 17:27.256
Wyck. What are you doing here?

17:27.756 --> 17:29.091
- Something wrong?
- No.

17:29.174 --> 17:32.678
No, I'm, uh, working with the mayor
on something and I…

17:33.971 --> 17:36.557
I was wondering if I could get
your eye on it?

17:36.640 --> 17:38.058
Oh, you're working with the mayor?

17:38.141 --> 17:39.852
- Well, that's new.
- [Wyck, chuckling] Yeah.

17:39.935 --> 17:41.687
I don't like it either, but, uh…

17:42.479 --> 17:44.690
[sighs] You think you could
take a look? It's…

17:45.190 --> 17:46.650
- Yeah.
- It's important.

17:46.733 --> 17:47.734
Of course, yeah.

17:47.818 --> 17:49.820
Found it in Bryce's rectory.

17:49.903 --> 17:50.988
- Oh.
- Yeah.

17:51.488 --> 17:52.489
[Gerrie] Okay.

17:54.533 --> 17:55.534
[sniffs]

17:57.035 --> 17:58.036
Yeah.

17:59.079 --> 18:00.080
How have you been?

18:01.039 --> 18:02.040
Fine.

18:03.458 --> 18:06.837
Okay. Saving it for the memoir, I see.

18:08.589 --> 18:13.802
My father… [chuckles] …used to say
that you were too chatty.

18:13.886 --> 18:16.096
[both chuckling]

18:17.472 --> 18:18.891
[Wyck] Yeah, he never liked me.

18:18.974 --> 18:21.310
[Gerrie chuckles]
Well, you kept me out too late.

18:22.144 --> 18:23.353
Oh, that's interesting.

18:23.437 --> 18:25.147
- Let me… Let me put it on the…
- Yeah.

18:27.149 --> 18:28.150
Put on the light.

18:31.486 --> 18:32.821
- Okay.
- [Wyck] All right.

18:33.989 --> 18:35.240
[Gerrie] All right.

18:35.324 --> 18:38.243
"I do not comprehend the nature
of the curse

18:38.327 --> 18:40.787
that has fallen on the island.

18:41.330 --> 18:45.125
I do know that its heart beats
inside the cylinder

18:45.626 --> 18:48.045
that my husband wears around his neck.

18:48.128 --> 18:53.091
Who will crush my throat?
His hands? This plague?

18:53.175 --> 18:57.596
Death comes for each of us,
but I fear to me first.

18:57.679 --> 18:59.973
I know not how, but who.

19:01.099 --> 19:05.312
Of course, he's here with me,
so I say all of this in jest,

19:05.395 --> 19:07.272
and with that, I retire."

19:09.691 --> 19:10.692
That's…

19:12.194 --> 19:13.195
No.

19:23.830 --> 19:25.040
[Dale] Tom?

19:27.125 --> 19:28.252
Are you okay?

19:30.879 --> 19:33.298
- [Tom] I have to stop him.
- I have to stop him.

19:34.049 --> 19:37.761
- [Tom] I-I can't let…
- I-I can't let them overturn the curfew.

19:37.845 --> 19:39.096
…the curfew…

19:41.723 --> 19:43.851
[chair creaking]

19:46.395 --> 19:47.396
Oh.

19:53.861 --> 19:55.863
[low thrumming]

19:59.950 --> 20:01.618
[distorted] I think they're meeting soon.

20:01.702 --> 20:04.705
[chair creaking]

20:12.004 --> 20:13.005
You okay?

20:13.714 --> 20:17.092
[chair creaking]

20:32.024 --> 20:33.066
[chuckles]

20:35.777 --> 20:38.071
[lights crackling, echoing]

20:39.948 --> 20:41.658
You're goddamn right we're mad!

20:41.742 --> 20:44.244
- We've poured our blood, sweat, tears…
- [townspeople clamoring]

20:44.328 --> 20:49.499
…and a hell of a lot of money into trying
to make this "the next Martha's Vineyard."

20:49.583 --> 20:51.668
And the crazy thing is, it is working.

20:51.752 --> 20:56.089
It is actually happening,
and you are destroying it for what?

20:56.173 --> 20:58.133
- [townspeople muttering]
- [person] For what?

20:58.217 --> 20:59.551
For what?

20:59.635 --> 21:00.844
For what? For what?

21:05.265 --> 21:09.144
You can't keep people locked indoors
while the sun is still up, Loftis.

21:09.228 --> 21:10.395
[townspeople muttering]

21:10.479 --> 21:12.689
People come here for the outdoor stuff.

21:12.773 --> 21:14.525
Beaches a-a-and sunshine.

21:14.608 --> 21:18.570
Not to spend all day
in my piece of shit hotel!

21:18.654 --> 21:21.573
- [townspeople] Mm-hmm.
- It's okay! My piece of shit hotel!

21:21.657 --> 21:23.200
It sucks! I know it sucks!

21:23.784 --> 21:26.328
It's sucked for 25 years!
That's why I don't live there!

21:26.828 --> 21:30.374
I say fuck the moratoriums,

21:30.457 --> 21:32.334
- fuck the curfews.
- [townspeople] Yep.

21:32.417 --> 21:33.961
- I want more tourists.
- I'm ready.

21:34.503 --> 21:37.130
[Kurt] I want more money
coming into the island!

21:37.214 --> 21:38.423
- [person 2] Yes.
- [person 3] Right.

21:38.507 --> 21:42.594
And we sure as fuck aren't canceling
the fucking fireworks!

21:42.678 --> 21:44.638
That's right! That's right, Kurt!

21:44.721 --> 21:48.350
- [townspeople applauding]
- [Wayne] Hold it! Hold it!

21:48.433 --> 21:49.977
Hold it, hold it!

21:50.060 --> 21:52.855
I wanna hear from Loftis!

21:52.938 --> 21:55.315
Let's hear what he has to say!

22:03.448 --> 22:04.449
[gasps]

22:18.755 --> 22:21.133
[janitor] Oh, someone's got a full belly.

22:21.884 --> 22:23.260
You had a lot to eat today?

22:26.638 --> 22:27.639
You okay, boss?

22:41.904 --> 22:43.071
[sighs] There you are!

22:44.531 --> 22:46.491
- [PJ laughs]
- [Evan] It's categorically not correct.

22:46.575 --> 22:49.244
- Okay?
- [PJ] I'm s… I'm serious dude.

22:49.745 --> 22:50.871
It's true.

22:50.954 --> 22:53.498
- It's true, my uncle doesn't lie to me.
- Wait, what is that?

22:53.582 --> 22:54.583
What?

22:56.293 --> 22:58.170
[teen 2] I think I saw
something in the window.

22:58.253 --> 23:00.255
[faint rock music playing on radio]

23:00.339 --> 23:02.341
[teen 1] I just think you're really high.

23:02.424 --> 23:04.426
[all snickering]

23:05.802 --> 23:07.596
It's okay. [chuckles]

23:08.972 --> 23:10.307
Don't worry, I'll protect you.

23:10.849 --> 23:12.518
- Oh, really?
- [chuckling] Yeah.

23:13.018 --> 23:15.771
[in deep voice] I'll protect you.
Mr. Brave Guy.

23:15.854 --> 23:17.231
[PJ] Ooh, brave guy.

23:17.314 --> 23:18.649
- Okay. No.
- [chuckles]

23:19.483 --> 23:21.276
Well, you know, you know what they say.

23:21.944 --> 23:23.570
Anyone that goes in doesn't come out.

23:25.072 --> 23:26.114
I bet you won't.

23:32.037 --> 23:34.831
- [PJ, Gil, teen 2 exclaim]
- [teen 1] Oh, my God! Okay.

23:34.915 --> 23:37.376
- [teen 2] Whoa.
- [Evan] Let's see it. [chuckles]

23:38.043 --> 23:41.088
- Come on, I think that's pretty good.
- [teen 2 clucking]

23:42.089 --> 23:44.591
- [teen 1] He's not gonna do it.
- He's gonna pretend like he's hot shit.

23:44.675 --> 23:45.759
He's gonna like throw himself--

23:45.843 --> 23:47.386
- [Evan screams]
- [all exclaim]

23:47.469 --> 23:48.971
Didn't work on me, didn't work.

23:49.054 --> 23:51.306
- He's gonna be…
- [teen 1] Yes, it did. I saw you jump.

23:51.390 --> 23:52.474
You did.

23:52.558 --> 23:55.143
[PJ] Come on, buddy. Come on, pal.

23:55.227 --> 23:56.895
- Yeah, there he goes.
- [teen 1] Oh, dude.

23:56.979 --> 23:58.105
- That's right.
- He's still going.

23:58.188 --> 23:59.189
[ominous music plays]

23:59.273 --> 24:01.149
[crackling, echoing]

24:01.233 --> 24:05.988
[Gerrie] Right? And… Yeah. Sorry-Sorry
about the, uh, math teacher coffee breath.

24:06.071 --> 24:07.656
[Patricia] Oh, I didn't catch a whiff.

24:07.739 --> 24:09.575
[Gerrie] Oh, good. Um, the… So…

24:10.367 --> 24:12.452
There is… well, there is no-no year here,

24:12.536 --> 24:15.831
but what caught my interest was
right here.

24:15.914 --> 24:17.708
The reference to a plague.

24:18.709 --> 24:21.545
There's only been one plague
in Widow's Bay and that was in 1702.

24:21.628 --> 24:25.257
- [Wyck] Mm-hmm.
- So, right, I took a swing.

24:27.843 --> 24:28.844
There it is.

24:31.305 --> 24:32.389
[gasps]

24:33.891 --> 24:35.267
- [hand thuds]
- Isn't that something?

24:35.350 --> 24:36.852
[Gerrie] Yes, Sarah Westcott Warren.

24:36.935 --> 24:38.145
Where am I?

24:39.313 --> 24:40.606
You seen anything yet?

24:43.192 --> 24:45.235
Okay, well, uh,
we're on to something, Tom,

24:45.319 --> 24:47.279
so, just, uh, hold on a second.

24:47.362 --> 24:48.780
[stammers] Use your crayons.

24:48.864 --> 24:50.324
Yeah, and, um…

24:50.407 --> 24:53.952
She married Richard Warren,
our founding father, that year.

24:54.036 --> 24:57.289
And here, this. This reference here
about the cylinder he wears?

24:57.372 --> 24:58.874
This "cursed" item?

24:58.957 --> 25:00.167
[stammers]

25:00.250 --> 25:01.835
What is this? What does that look like?

25:01.919 --> 25:05.422
Well, if you give me a paintbrush,
I can tell you whatever you need to know.

25:05.506 --> 25:07.716
Yeah, that's great Tom. What is it, Wyck?

25:07.799 --> 25:10.928
I'm wondering if he could've been
buried with it.

25:11.011 --> 25:12.346
[Patricia] The cylinder?

25:12.429 --> 25:15.933
- [gulls cawing, echoing]
- [Tom] Evan? Ev… Evan? Evan?

25:16.850 --> 25:17.893
Where's my son?

25:20.020 --> 25:22.231
Where's Evan? Where's my son?

25:22.314 --> 25:24.358
- Okay, take it easy.
- Where-Where is Evan?

25:24.441 --> 25:26.693
[Patricia] Just sit-sit down, Tom.

25:26.777 --> 25:27.861
Sit.

25:28.529 --> 25:29.738
Sit.

25:29.821 --> 25:30.989
Down. Sit!

25:31.573 --> 25:33.909
Tom! Tom! Tom!

25:33.992 --> 25:35.077
[grunts] Tom!

25:35.911 --> 25:36.954
[gasps]

25:37.037 --> 25:38.664
[sultry music playing on radio]

25:38.747 --> 25:40.624
- [Tom spluttering]
- [Rosemary] Hey.

25:41.166 --> 25:43.961
Only lap belts back there, buckle up.

25:44.044 --> 25:45.045
Um…

25:46.296 --> 25:48.090
I-I-I have to find Evan.

25:48.715 --> 25:51.844
Well, I hope he's at your house,

25:51.927 --> 25:54.137
'cause that's where they told me
to take you.

25:54.221 --> 25:55.514
[Tom] Oh, thank God.

25:55.597 --> 25:57.140
I just need to make one little stop.

25:57.224 --> 26:00.394
- What? No, no, please. No.
- Only gonna take a second.

26:00.477 --> 26:02.020
- No! Rosemary, no!
- One--

26:07.609 --> 26:09.611
[insects chirping]

26:16.618 --> 26:17.619
[horn beeps]

26:19.162 --> 26:20.163
[Tom grunts]

26:32.759 --> 26:35.762
[slow pop music playing on speakers]

26:40.559 --> 26:42.561
[bell chiming]

26:48.775 --> 26:50.694
Don't move the car again, Tom.

26:52.404 --> 26:56.158
Ha! Just won 15 bucks! Yes!

26:56.742 --> 26:58.744
[vacuum whirring]

27:07.586 --> 27:08.962
[Tom] That's my loafer.

27:10.297 --> 27:11.590
No, no, no!

27:11.673 --> 27:14.426
I told you to get out! Get out!

27:14.927 --> 27:15.969
No, no, no!

27:23.977 --> 27:25.979
[eerie music playing]

27:51.296 --> 27:53.298
[door creaking]

28:00.430 --> 28:04.268
[Bechir, on loudspeaker] Evan Loftis.
Please step away from the creepy house.

28:04.893 --> 28:05.894
[chuckles]

28:06.645 --> 28:09.815
- This isn't my house? Oh. My-My bad.
- [friends snickering]

28:09.898 --> 28:11.567
- [Bechir] Boy, get over here.
- I…

28:11.650 --> 28:12.651
Thank God.

28:12.734 --> 28:14.111
[friends laugh]

28:20.242 --> 28:24.204
Hi. Um, I'm-I'm sorry.

28:24.288 --> 28:27.666
We-We have some off-island girls
in the… in the car,

28:27.749 --> 28:30.419
and I-I just… We were just
trying to impress them.

28:30.502 --> 28:31.503
Hmm.

28:32.004 --> 28:33.964
Yeah. Yeah, no, I get it.

28:35.048 --> 28:37.676
Breaking and entering is very impressive.

28:40.137 --> 28:41.889
Please don't tell my dad.

28:44.433 --> 28:47.019
Fine, but go ahead and get outta here.

28:47.102 --> 28:48.520
Okay. Thank you.

28:49.313 --> 28:50.314
Um, uh…

28:52.274 --> 28:55.903
Just-just while I'm walking away, can, I…

28:55.986 --> 28:59.656
Can I just yell "Fuck you, pig"
for the girls?

29:01.867 --> 29:03.410
No, the fuck, you cannot.

29:03.493 --> 29:04.661
Okay. Okay.

29:04.745 --> 29:07.122
[stammers] Bye.

29:07.748 --> 29:09.541
- [grunts]
- [friends laugh]

29:11.335 --> 29:13.545
[chuckles]

29:14.796 --> 29:16.798
[rock music playing on radio]

29:19.301 --> 29:21.303
[teenagers exclaiming, laughing]

29:23.472 --> 29:24.473
[PJ] Oh, shit.

29:29.520 --> 29:30.687
[radio stops]

29:37.027 --> 29:38.862
The fuck is going on with your dad, dude?

29:39.404 --> 29:40.489
That's your dad?

29:42.407 --> 29:43.659
[Evan] What's up? What's up?

29:51.124 --> 29:53.418
[teen 2] Oh, my God. [breathes heavily]

29:58.507 --> 30:00.008
[glass squeaking]

30:00.092 --> 30:02.386
[PJ] Yo, I think your dad
is looking for you.

30:10.102 --> 30:13.772
[squeaking continues]

30:19.361 --> 30:20.654
- I gotta go. Go.
- Okay.

30:21.154 --> 30:24.032
Get inside, right now.
And say good night to little…

30:25.742 --> 30:26.743
miss.

30:30.080 --> 30:31.790
You better start explaining yourself
right--

30:31.874 --> 30:33.500
- Fuck you!
- What did you say?

30:34.001 --> 30:35.919
What did you… What did you just say?

30:43.260 --> 30:44.761
I had fun tonight.

30:45.554 --> 30:46.930
I had a good time.

30:49.558 --> 30:52.644
And if you had it your way, I would've sat
in your shitty office all day.

30:52.728 --> 30:54.646
Evan, do you think I want to be

30:54.730 --> 30:56.940
- watching you the whole fucking time?
- No, no, I… No, I don't!

30:57.024 --> 31:00.444
No, I think… I think you wanna show people
that you can control me.

31:01.361 --> 31:02.362
What?

31:04.865 --> 31:08.785
The reason you're a shitty mayor
is not because of me, okay?

31:11.830 --> 31:14.333
- [low thrumming]
- [liquid gurgling]

31:14.416 --> 31:15.417
[scoffs]

31:16.376 --> 31:18.754
[echoing] I think… I think… I think

31:18.837 --> 31:20.380
[normal] you're gonna feel very guilty

31:20.464 --> 31:22.132
for saying that to me one day.

31:26.970 --> 31:28.555
Why do we never leave this island?

31:29.056 --> 31:30.057
[sighs]

31:32.935 --> 31:34.436
What kind of fucking parenting is that?

31:34.520 --> 31:36.939
It was important to your mother that,
um, that you be raised here.

31:37.022 --> 31:38.815
What? Never go anywhere?
That's what she wanted?

31:38.899 --> 31:40.234
We'll continue this in the morning.

31:45.280 --> 31:46.281
Dad!

31:47.157 --> 31:48.158
Dad!

31:48.242 --> 31:51.995
Dad, one of these days, I'm gonna leave
and I'm never, ever coming back!

31:57.167 --> 31:59.169
- [fireworks popping]
- [grunts]

31:59.253 --> 32:01.547
[ominous music playing]

32:01.630 --> 32:02.631
[grunts]

32:03.465 --> 32:04.466
[coughs]

32:09.304 --> 32:10.514
[retches]

32:12.391 --> 32:14.017
[coughing]

32:16.144 --> 32:18.272
[retching]

32:21.650 --> 32:24.152
- [inhales sharply]
- [fireworks continue]

32:24.236 --> 32:25.696
[sighs, pants]

32:26.196 --> 32:27.197
[echoing] Are you ready?

32:29.157 --> 32:30.200
Are you ready?

32:30.284 --> 32:32.494
[ominous music playing]

32:33.203 --> 32:34.204
[normal] Are you ready?

32:42.921 --> 32:44.923
[retching]

32:45.632 --> 32:47.426
[Tom, echoing] Lauren? Lauren? Lauren?

32:53.807 --> 32:56.059
[gulls cawing]

32:58.228 --> 32:59.229
I can't see anything.

33:02.983 --> 33:06.111
- [echoing] Lauren? Lauren?
- [breathing shakily]

33:07.529 --> 33:10.449
- [echoing] Lauren? Lauren?
- I can't… I can't see anything!

33:10.532 --> 33:11.617
I can't see anything!

33:11.700 --> 33:13.660
[stammers] I need some help here, please!

33:13.744 --> 33:16.705
Can you please turn the boat around?
Turn the… Turn the boat around.

33:16.788 --> 33:18.123
Turn it n-now! Now!

33:18.207 --> 33:19.917
[Tom] Lauren? Lauren?

33:20.000 --> 33:22.002
[ominous music continues]

33:25.172 --> 33:26.173
[hospital monitor beeps]

33:26.256 --> 33:28.258
- The baby is just fine.
- [sighs]

33:28.342 --> 33:32.054
- [beeping continues]
- Okay. But-But what about her?

33:32.137 --> 33:33.514
[stammers] She… She seems…

33:34.890 --> 33:35.974
off.

33:36.558 --> 33:38.185
[doctor] Just give it some time.

33:42.731 --> 33:43.732
Hello.

33:52.616 --> 33:53.867
[sighs, inhales sharply]

33:59.039 --> 34:01.041
[panting]

34:04.044 --> 34:09.257
Please, oh, God, if you can hear me,

34:10.092 --> 34:11.885
if-if you exist…

34:14.429 --> 34:16.348
ple-please help me.

34:17.474 --> 34:18.641
Please. Please help me.

34:18.725 --> 34:20.768
Please, please protect my son.

34:23.355 --> 34:25.023
Please protect my son.

34:25.107 --> 34:26.108
[sniffles]

34:26.190 --> 34:27.192
[music stops]

34:28.235 --> 34:29.610
I'll do anything.

34:38.203 --> 34:41.831
[entity speaking indistinctly]

34:48.130 --> 34:51.049
[entity continues, intensifies]

35:14.656 --> 35:16.658
["Amber" playing]
